  "facts": [
    "The Tunnel de la Croix-Rousse opened its first roadway on 19 April 1952, spanning 1,782 meters to link Lyon’s Rhône and Saône rivers across the Croix-Rousse hill.",
    "In 1999, a central wall was added to the two‑lane tunnel, finally separating the traffic flows that previously shared a single roadway.",
    "A 2013 sustainable transport tunnel opened beside the car tunnel, illuminating cyclists and pedestrians with colored lights, video displays, and music for a unique travel experience."
